/-
# Cambridge Part III Benchmark — MiniConnectedness

Benchmark problems at the Cambridge Part III (graduate) level
covering connectedness in point-set topology.
-/

import MiniConnectedness

open MiniConnectedness

#eval "══ CAMBRIDGE PART III BENCHMARK ══"

/-! ### Problem 1: Connected Components of Q -/
#eval "Show that Q is totally disconnected. Prove that the only connected subsets of Q are singletons."

/-! ### Problem 2: Product of Connected Spaces -/
#eval "Prove that an arbitrary product of connected spaces is connected (Tychonoff product topology)."

/-! ### Problem 3: Closure of Connected -/
#eval "Prove: if A ⊆ X is connected, then cl(A) is connected. Show the converse fails."

/-! ### Problem 4: Locally Connected iff Components Open -/
#eval "Prove X is locally connected iff every connected component of every open set is open."

/-! ### Problem 5: Hahn-Mazurkiewicz -/
#eval "State and prove the Hahn-Mazurkiewicz theorem: X is a continuous image of [0,1] iff X is a Peano continuum."

/-! ### Problem 6: Continua Decomposition -/
#eval "Prove every continuum contains at least two non-cut points. Classify all continua with exactly two non-cut points."

#eval "══ CAMBRIDGE PART III BENCHMARK COMPLETE ══"
